            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the recent hospital admission of your 70-year-old female patient, who presented with an acute exacerbation of her known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, she exhibited significant dyspnoea, increased sputum production, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray confirmed pulmonary hyperinflation without pneumonic infiltrates. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed hypoxaemia with mild hypercapnia. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers consistent with an infective trigger. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and antibiotic coverage. Clinical response was satisfactory with improvement in respiratory function and oxygen saturation. She was discharged in stable condition with adjusted inhaler therapy and a short course of oral steroids. Please arrange follow-up within two weeks and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
